<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

A triple-backtick fence opening with the language token `toml` declares data inside a carrier. The fence takes an optional PROFILE name after that token, and the profile decides where the parsed table lands:

* ''`meta`'' — the carrier identity prelude. It dissolves into the parent tiddler's fields through `parseTaploFields`, so `uri-path`, `mana`, `source-file` and their kin read as tiddler fields and answer the `toml:` filter operator directly.
* ''any other name, or none'' — a general-purpose data block. The content stays available to the widget layer and lands in no field.

`sigil-toml.tid` declares the surface with `lar-kind: data` and `lar-render: mark`: the fence marks a region for the compile layer rather than rendering an element of its own.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/parser>>

!! Parser

`smol-toml`, vendored at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/lib-smol-toml.ts` and reachable in the wiki as `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/lib/smol-toml`. `parseTaploFields` in `toml-ast.ts` runs the sync TOML→flat-record read that the deserializer calls when it splits a carrier into its records.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

